		heading: 'What love means in the Bible',
		bodyHtml: `<p>Biblical love is <strong>steady, self-giving goodwill</strong>. It is not only a warm feeling, though it includes feeling, and not only duty, though it includes commitment. It is a Father who keeps choosing His children&rsquo;s good. &ldquo;This is love: not that we loved our Father, but that he loved us and sent his Son as the atoning sacrifice for our sins&rdquo; (1 John 4:10).</p><p>That order matters. We do not earn love by loving well; we learn to love because we have been loved. &ldquo;Beloved, let us love one another, for love is from our Father, and all who love are born of him and know him&rdquo; (1 John 4:7).</p>`,
	},
